.SS "Académie Franc C’Aise"
.PP
\fIAcadémie Franc C'Aise\fP is the \fIfunctional tester\fP made in \fIPython\fP for
the \fIFranc C\fP, and uses \fILarousse\fP standard library.

.PP
You will find in every single \fILarousse\fP source code function: - The
same function written in \fIC\fP. - A main function in \fIFranc C\fP which calls
the function in \fIFranc C\fP with various parameter, in the \fItest\fP
folder. - A main function in \fIC\fP which calls the function in \fIC\fP with
the same parameters, in the \fItest\fP folder.

.PP
\fIAcadémie Franc C'Aise\fP compiles both the \fIC\fP and \fIFranc C\fP version
using \fIgcc\fP and \fIfcvm\fP. It then runs both versions, and check whether
their inputs are the same as a way to test the language. It also
displays how much time each step took (Compilation, Execution) for both
languages then finally shows the time difference between those.

.PP
\fIFranc C\fP is in most cases faster to compile than \fIC\fP. However, \fIC\fP is
almost always faster in execution time than \fIFranc C\fP.

.PP
At the end of the program, \fIAcadémie Franc C'Aise\fP displays how many
tests passed out of how many were run. It then exits with a failure if
not all tests passed.
